  "reset_roster_policy": "Exactly13 unique readable non-command registers; all defined bits including CR1.ACCESS/WINDOW compared with own reset. No KEY or ICR reads. TIME/ALARMA/ALARMB reset0x00120000; AWTARR0xFFFF. This is a deliberately conservative software contract.",
  "read_policy": "Controls first and reject on mismatch before COMPEN/calendar reads; repeat entire snapshot. No WINDOW wait, ACCESS, KEY, reset, flag clear or RTC write during RCC admission.",
  "wake_policy": "Own PDF178: raw RTCCLK wake sources0..3 need not have START; sources4..7 require RTC1Hz and START. START=0 alone is insufficient.",
  "compensation_policy": "Own PDF174 Table12-3 allows compensated LSE 1Hz with SOURCE ignored; any nonreset snapshot across every SOURCE blocks disabled-source startup.",
  "retention_policy": "Own PDF172 explicitly preserves RTC counting/registers over non-POR resets. Enabled exact source reuse bypasses new-source consumer admission and never rewrites retained RTC; a new source start requires pristine state and never manufactures it.",
  "calendar_policy": "Own PDF173 §12.3.5 permits matching consecutive TIME or DATE reads. Bounded T-D-T-D-T is a software snapshot strategy, not an atomic rollover or post-fault continuity guarantee. Held-source health checks before and after attach/now remain.",
  "no_claims": [
    "No automatic LSE request inferred from SDK silence.",
    "No RTC migration, reset, compensation setup, low-power support or clock-fault recovery.",
    "No silicon execution or crystal waveform/accuracy guarantee."
  ],
